A warm, aromatic twist on traditional holiday cranberry sauce. Sweetened dried cranberries plump up in simmering cranberry juice alongside diced Gala apples and woodsy cinnamon, gently thickened into a glossy jewel-toned spread.

*Adapted from [Aaron McCargo Jr. / Food Network](http://www.foodnetwork.com/recipes/aaron-mccargo-jr/cinnamon-apple-cranberry-sauce-recipe-1949092).*

## Ingredients

- 2 cups cranberry juice (100% juice or cranberry cocktail)
- 1 package (6 oz) sweetened dried cranberries
- 1 whole cinnamon stick, snapped in half
- 1 cup granulated sugar
- 2 Gala apples, peeled, cored, and cut into ¼-inch dice
- 2 teaspoons cornstarch

## Instructions

1. **Simmer the Cranberry Base:** Set a medium saucepan over medium heat. Add the cranberry juice, dried cranberries, halved cinnamon stick, and granulated sugar. Stir until the sugar dissolves. Bring the mixture to a gentle boil, then let it simmer for 5 minutes to allow the cranberries to begin absorbing the warm liquid.
2. **Incorporate the Diced Apples:** Add the peeled and diced Gala apples into the saucepan. Continue simmering over medium-low heat for roughly 5 minutes, giving it a stir every minute or two, until the apples have slightly softened but still retain their shape.
3. **Whisk the Slurry:** Carefully ladle out 1 cup (8 fl oz) of the hot cooking liquid into a heatproof bowl or measuring cup. Add the 2 teaspoons of cornstarch and whisk briskly with a small whisk or fork until no lumps remain.
4. **Thicken the Sauce:** Pour the cornstarch slurry back into the saucepan in a steady stream, stirring constantly. Cook at a low simmer for another 5 minutes; the sauce will clarify, turn deeply ruby-red, and thicken to a rich glaze.
5. **Cool and Chill to Set:** Take the pan off the heat and transfer the sauce into a heat-safe glass serving dish. Refrigerate for at least 30 minutes (or overnight); the sauce will firm up and thicken further as it cools. Remove and discard the cinnamon sticks prior to serving.

## Notes

- **Apple Varieties:** Gala apples offer a mild, sweet profile that balances tart cranberry juice nicely. For a slightly tarter sauce with firmer apple bite, swap in Honeycrisp, Pink Lady, or Granny Smith apples.
- **Serving Suggestions:** Fantastic alongside roasted turkey, glazed ham, or pork roast. Also delicious spooned warm or chilled over baked brie with crusty baguette slices.
- **Storage:** Keeps exceptionally well in an airtight glass container in the refrigerator for up to 7 to 10 days.
